      "id": 1,
      "text": "Washington, New Jersey was incorporated as a borough on February 20, 1868, from portions of Washington Township.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington_Borough%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The borough was named for George Washington, one of over ten communities in New Jersey honoring the first president.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington_Borough%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "During the late 19th and early 20th centuries, Washington, New Jersey became a hub for musical instrument manufacturing, especially organs.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington_Borough%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Morris Canal and two rail lines of the Delaware, Lackawanna and Western Railroad significantly contributed to Washington, New Jersey's growth in the 19th century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington_Borough%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Washington, New Jersey is completely surrounded by Washington Township, making it one of the state's 'doughnut towns'.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington_Borough%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The borough's downtown area was revitalized after a major fire devastated it in 1962, leading to new residential and retail developments.",
